Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.23.1
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.23.1 fixes the still-broken corner resize. Archive 25 proved the resize recognizer fires (begin/end logged) but the window frame never changes by a single point; the drag-to-move gesture uses the identical translationInView pattern incrementally and works, so the only functional difference - the 0.22.0 anchor-at-start plus absolute-size rewrite - is reverted to the proven incremental model: each Changed projects the incremental pan onto the original bottom-right diagonal to get a single width delta, accumulates it into the current width (min 150 pt, clamped to screen), and derives height as width / locked aspect ratio so content still never distorts. A throttled Changed log (every 4th tick: translation, delta, resulting W/H) is added so the next log definitively separates no-Changed-events from changed-but-reverted. No config changes; cfgVersion stays 20.
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
